</style>
<h1>File format reference</h1>
<p>This page describes specialized PLINK 2.0 input and <a href="/plink/2.0/output">output</a> file formats which are identifiable by file extension.  (Most extensions not listed here have very simple one-entry-per-line or two-entry-per-line text formats.)</p>
<p>Unless otherwise specified, all multicolumn text files generated by PLINK 2.0 are tab-delimited, with one header line starting with '#'.  In the column summaries, columns which are present unless removed by the column set descriptor are <b>boldface</b>, and columns which only appear under some data/flag/modifier combination(s) are <i>italicized</i>.</p>
<p><b>Jump to:</b>
  <a href="#afreq">.acount</a> |
  <a href="#adjusted">.adjusted</a> |
  <a href="#afreq">.afreq</a> |
  <a href="#allele_no_snp">.allele.no.snp</a> |
